        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{91}{216}$",
          "worked": "Let $E$ be the event of rolling at least one 5 in the first three rolls. The complementary event is rolling no 5s. Each independent roll has probability $\\frac56$ of giving a number other than 5.\n\n$$\\begin{align*} P(E) &= 1-\\left(\\frac56\\right)^3 \\\\ P(E) &= 1-\\frac{125}{216} \\\\ P(E) &= \\frac{91}{216} \\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q14-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Write down a formula for the probability of rolling the number ‘5’ at least once in the first $n$ rolls of the die.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1-\\left(\\frac56\\right)^n$",
          "worked": "Let $E_n$ be the event of rolling at least one 5 in the first $n$ rolls. Multiply the probability of missing 5 across all $n$ independent rolls.\n\n$$\\begin{align*} P(E_n) &= 1-P(\\text{no 5 in the first }n\\text{ rolls}) \\\\ P(E_n) &= 1-\\left(\\frac56\\right)^n \\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q14-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p13-q14-c-task",
